{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394261-familiar-idea-involving-brawl","id":1394261,"title":"Familiar Idea involving Brawl","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-04T23:26:33-07:00","id":1394261,"title":"Familiar Idea involving Brawl","content":"Would it be suitable to have a charm in Survival that would allow one to use essence to enhance one's Familiar's attacks with your Brawl Charms?<br /> <br /> <b>Barging Claws of the Sun</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m or 10m, 1wp<br /> <b>Mins: </b>Survival 5, Brawl 3, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keyword: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>instant or one scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Bestial Traits Technique, Familiar-Honing Instruction<br /> <br /> The solar's anima engulfs her Familiar, and deepens their connection of essence, allowing the Solar to enhance her Familiar's attacks with Brawl charm she knows, and that are suitable for the attack in question. (No using clinch charms on a Familiar that has no clinch attack, for example). <br /> For 5m, this last for one attack, but for 10m, 1wp, this will last for an entire scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T00:41:56-07:00","id":1394273,"title":"","content":"Speaking as the ST of a Survival Supernal, no. It's not balanced at all. Nevermind that Cross-Skill charms are rare in 3e, this specific charm is going to crack the game. <br /> <br /> So there's two broad approaches to this: a Survival Superal with Brawl or a Brawler Supernal with Survival. Its only 9 charms to get Deadly Predator Method and its only 5 to get Saga Beast Virtue. Either of these on a Familiar \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Tyrant Lizard or Siege Lizard or River Dragon are already better then pretty much any threat below E3. Survival is very, very powerful. Finish out the Pokemon Tree of Survival and they are straight up Immune to Decisive Attacks. I have literally watched one of these break a Nephwrack + monster horde battle without taking damage. It was capable of Soloing some refluffed 2nd circle demons. They have a truckload of hp and very high resting defenses. Giving one of these creatures even basic Brawl charms like Thunderclap Rush Attack are gonna upset the apple cart. Heaven Thunder Hammer will turn your pet dinosaur into a anti-grav cannon. <br /> <br /> From the Brawl side, though, you've basically just given the Brawler a second, risk-free body to cheese every fight with. Every snake is now a god stranger with Dragon Coil. Solar Cross Counter on any decent soak animal defending you is going to take the Action Economy out behind the woodshed and beat it senseless. The Hammer On Iron line of charms is going to devastate any opponent and put them into wound penalties- and none of this will cost the Solar any combat resources. <br /> <br /> There's next to no reason to ever use the 5m version of this charm- getting a second brawler with its own healthpool and motes and willpower is insanely good at that price. Hell. Just for all the Onslaught Penalties Brawl can hand out you have effectively made evryone without an Onslaught Negator at defense 0 for the rest of the fight, right from turn 1. Look at what it takes in Craft to get Dual Magus Prana- a charm that lets you just avoid death one time. This is a way better version of that, and if yoir beloved pet dies\u2026 oh well. Train up another one. <br /> <br /> And if I was gonna really cheese it, i'd get 2 pets and Empower whichever one is in a better position. Or both. 20m 2 wp for what is essentially 3 Dawns is insane. And thats not even including all the Giant Birds you could use to break the game. There's an entire Lunar build designed to throw people so high they die from unstoppable fall damage. A Survival Brawler can do that inside of 6 charms, without even having to get off the couch.<br /> <br /> I really like the concept of Charmshare with a Familiar, but I think it would work best if you made it a lot stricter and a lot harder to cheese.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T03:36:34-07:00","id":1394293,"title":"","content":"While I appreciate your words, and comments, there's one point you might have misconstrued:<br /> &quot;There's next to no reason to ever use the 5m version of this charm- getting a second brawler with its own healthpool and motes and willpower is insanely good at that price. &quot;<br /> <br /> The Familiar doesn't get it's own motes, and is a drain on your own motes. YOU have to power up those Brawl Charms for your Familiar! Sure, you might get two brawlers, but the 10m, 1 wp is just for the setup. Now you have to spend twice as many motes for both of them to gain the same benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:40:44-07:00","id":1394336,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s mostly okay, if you use Saga Beast Virtue, Deadly Predator Method and Barging Claws of the Sun all together that\u2019s 30m 3wp, and uses your first turn in combat. Combined with artifact weapons/armor and a full excellency on both you and your familiars join battle rolls that leaves you with six motes left to enhance your familiar\u2019s first attack, assuming you\u2019re Essence 3. After that you\u2019re relying on more drip for combat and no motes at all out of combat, in addition to being down three willpower. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, there\u2019s some familiars/charms that it\u2019s probably just too strong with. Even without motes charms like Heaven Fury Smite and Supremacy of War Meditation are free, and charms like Fivefold Fury Onslaught combined with a few other charms, and something like a claw strider is just too good. I\u2019d maybe keep it to only Supplemental charms to try and reign it in, but there might not be enough supplemental charms to make it worth it at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T08:04:52-07:00","id":1394348,"title":"","content":"I'd stick to a very specific list of brawl charms. Two onslaught lockers is probably too much, for example, but adding onslaught to raw damage should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:35:57-07:00","id":1394390,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> you've got a specific list in mind? I'm more than willing to hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T15:47:49-07:00","id":1394644,"title":"","content":"You're mostly stuck with the E1-2 range.<br /> <br /> For example, Iron Battle Focus, Ferocious Jab, Devil-Strangling Attitude, Blade-Rebuking Wrath. A onslaught defense, a damage enhancer, a grabber gets extra grabby, and anyone foolish enough to stab your cat will lose his sword and maybe his hand.<br /> <br /> The charm that turns these on needs not be too expensive either. 4m, scene or 5m scene is plenty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 06-06-2020, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T02:28:17-07:00","id":1395040,"title":"","content":"I think there's probably scope for something like an Essence 3 Charm that unlocks Essence 1 Brawl Charms for something like 5m/scene, an Essence 4 upgrade that unlocks Essence 2 Charms for a 1WP surcharge, and an Essence 5 repurchase that unlocks Essence 3 Brawl Charms for 10m 1WP 1a. If it costs revealing you are Anathema then that is pretty significant.<br /> <br /> Essence 3 Brawl on a Tyrant Lizard backed by Survival Charms is pretty wild. But if it requires Essence 5/Brawl Supernal AND anima then it should be pretty wild.<br /> <br /> (I do disagree with DrLoveMonkey's assessment. If you are heavily invested in Brawl and Familiar/Survival then you <i>probably</i> don't also have two Artifacts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T12:47:35-07:00","id":1395131,"title":"","content":"I think using Charms through your familiar should only be possible when you're disembodying yourself to possess and control the familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T07:31:38-07:00","id":1395343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394261-familiar-idea-involving-brawl?p=1395131#post1395131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think using Charms through your familiar should only be possible when you're disembodying yourself to possess and control the familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow both. The latter, of course, is a lot more permissive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T19:35:37-07:00","id":1395503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394261-familiar-idea-involving-brawl?p=1395040#post1395040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I do disagree with DrLoveMonkey's assessment. If you are heavily invested in Brawl and Familiar/Survival then you <i>probably</i> don't also have two Artifacts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that getting an artifact is more or less an inevitability of Exalted stories. Eventually you're going to raid a lost tomb, fight the wyld hunt, capture a fae noble, etc. It may nkt be the one you want, but its there. By E3 I'd be surprised if you didn't have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T05:33:56-07:00","id":1395583,"title":"","content":"In my experience such artifacts are neglected, and don't really matter for the discussion at hand. In a couple games I have seen them literally being discarded or pawned off for a political favor.<br /> <br /> <br /> Leave it to the exalted to scoff at such precious treasures <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T07:35:03-07:00","id":1395591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1394261-familiar-idea-involving-brawl?p=1395503#post1395503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find that getting an artifact is more or less an inevitability of Exalted stories. Eventually you're going to raid a lost tomb, fight the wyld hunt, capture a fae noble, etc. It may nkt be the one you want, but its there. By E3 I'd be surprised if you didn't have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Opens mouth to disagree*<br /> *The one PC in my game who deliberately didn't take an Artifact acquired one on Session 4*<br /> *Closes mouth*<br /> <br /> Still though... two Artifacts? On a Brawler? With a Familiar?<br /> <br /> One Artifact, sure, it happens.<br /> Two Artifacts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}